course: dictionary
lesson: 13411
title: Hickory: a tree, a wood, or a smell
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Hickory is a noun, so it names a thing. It can mean a tree, the hard wood from that tree, or the smoke from burning that wood. Context tells you which one. Ask yourself what the sentence is about before you choose a meaning.
explain: «We cracked hickory nuts on the back step.» Nuts grow on a tree, so here hickory means the tree that grows hard nuts. Read the words around the word: cracked and nuts are the clues.
explain: «The axe handle was made of hickory, so it did not snap.» The words «made of» tell you hickory is a material, the very hard, strong wood. The clue «did not snap» shows why that wood was chosen.
explain: «Dad bought hickory-smoked bacon.» The hyphen joins hickory and smoked, so the bacon was flavoured with smoke from hickory wood. Check your meaning by putting it in the sentence: it still makes sense.
fact: Hickory is a noun. Its plural is hickories.
fact: A hickory is a North American tree of the walnut family, with hard nuts.
fact: Hickory wood is very hard and strong, so it is used for tool handles and drumsticks.
fact: «Hickory» can also mean the smoke from hickory wood, which is used to flavour meat.
fact: In the nursery rhyme «Hickory, dickory, dock», hickory is one of the rhyming words.
exercise: «We cracked hickory nuts on the back step.» What is hickory here? | A kind of bacon | A stick for playing drums | *A tree that grows hard nuts | A nursery rhyme
exercise: «The axe handle was made of hickory, so it did not snap.» What does hickory mean? | *The very hard, strong wood of a tree | A squirrel that hides nuts | Smoke from burning wood | A type of bread
exercise: «The bacon tasted smoky because it was hickory-smoked.» What does hickory-smoked mean? | Cooked on a snowy day | *Flavoured with smoke from hickory wood | Left out in the sun to dry | Made of soft paper
test: Which word is the plural of hickory? | hickoryes | hickoris | hickorys | *hickories
test: Dad says «The barbecue smelled of hickory.» What does the smell most likely come from? | A pile of fallen leaves | Fresh cut grass | *Smoke from burning hickory wood | A bakery
exam: «The drummer tapped his hickory sticks.» What are hickory sticks? | A broken branch from a walnut tree | *Drumsticks made of hard hickory wood | Long sticks of sweets | Empty hickory nut shells
